From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: data the GPU's engines write keeps its pages tracked (EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED, off unless set)

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii 6cd99d2e15 (PR #1436, "buffer_cache: data the GPU's engines write keeps
its pages tracked"), by Zortos (zortos293), from Lucas Borges' (lucastaonline) #1161 (4c44094e30),
with Copilot and capy-ai. Ported against our patched buffer cache (series up to 0971); the
upstream memory tracker test is not taken.

What: inline constant buffer data the GPU's own engines write (MemoryManager::WriteBlockCached ->
FlushCaching -> RasterizerVulkan::InnerInvalidation -> BufferCache::WriteMemory) was marked like a
guest CPU write: the pages became CPU-modified AND untracked (a host protection change), and the
next upload tracked them again (another). With EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED=1, where the written
pages hold no GPU-written data, such a write sets the CPU bits but leaves the pages tracked
(WordManager::MarkWrittenTracked / MemoryTracker::MarkRegionAsWrittenTracked): the upload clears
the bits and has nothing to track again. Pages with GPU-written data take the old mark (after the
download our WriteMemory already does). Upstream measured ~4% of the GPU thread at Ocarina of
Time's village water, 60.9 fps against 59.5 (PC, author's 3 interleaved rounds).

Differences from upstream, for our tree: no ForgetSynchronized/NoteCleanWord (not in our tracker);
instead upload_epoch and cpu_epoch move (so the full-region clean shortcut and the uniform
memoisation see the write, as ChangeRegionState does) and, under EDEN_UP_HOT_PAGES, the hot page
clean bit is dropped so this frame's upload still sends the new bytes. The GPU-written check is
taken before our keep_page_gpu_data download (which removes the ranges it downloads).

Count line (stderr): "EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED writes N kept tracked, pages P stayed tracked,
F engine writes on GPU-written pages marked as before" at the first such write, then every 65536th;
P counts pages that were tracked and stayed so (each a protection change and its undo saved).
"EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED on" once at first use.

Unset: every write marks as before (InnerInvalidation passes engine_write, which is ignored).
Store: buffer cache, memory tracker, word manager and vk_rasterizer.cpp are not translation id
inputs: KEEPS THE STORE.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index afc5abb74b..48244e5252 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -480,8 +480,50 @@ void BufferCache<P>::UnmapGPUMemory(size_t as_id, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, size_t size
     }
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED=1 (off by default; zortos293/Lichii #1436, 6cd99d2e15, Zortos,
+// from Lucas Borges' #1161): data the GPU's own engines wrote (inline constant buffer data,
+// MemoryManager::FlushCaching -> InnerInvalidation) marks its pages CPU-modified but leaves them
+// tracked, where the pages hold no GPU-written data. A guest CPU mark untracks the pages (a host
+// protection change) and the next upload tracks them again (another), for writes no guest CPU
+// access needed to see; upstream measured ~4% of the GPU thread at Ocarina of Time's village water,
+// 60.9 fps against 59.5. A guest CPU access to such a page takes the tracked path, as for any
+// tracked page. Unset: every write marks as before.
+inline bool EngineTrackedOn() noexcept {
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const bool value = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED");
+        if (value) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED on: engine writes keep their pages "
+                                 "tracked\n");
+        }
+        return value;
+    }();
+    return on;
+}
+
+// A stderr line at the first engine write kept tracked, then every 65536th: writes kept tracked,
+// pages that stayed tracked (each one a protection change and its undo saved), and engine writes
+// that took the old mark because their pages held GPU-written data.
+inline void NoteEngineTracked(bool kept, u64 pages) noexcept {
+    static std::atomic<u64> writes{0}, kept_pages{0}, fallbacks{0};
+    if (!kept) {
+        fallbacks.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        return;
+    }
+    const u64 total = kept_pages.fetch_add(pages, std::memory_order_relaxed) + pages;
+    const u64 count = writes.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+    if (count == 1 || (count & 0xFFFF) == 0) {
+        std::fprintf(stderr,
+                     "EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED writes %llu kept tracked, pages %llu stayed "
+                     "tracked, %llu engine writes on GPU-written pages marked as before\n",
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(count),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(total),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(fallbacks.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)));
+    }
+}
+
 template <class P>
-void BufferCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool keep_page_gpu_data) {
+void BufferCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool keep_page_gpu_data,
+                                 bool engine_write) {
     Nx2NoteListHostWrite(device_addr, size);
     NoteUniformWrite(device_addr, size); // EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP; nothing unless set
     if (IsRegionGpuModified(device_addr, size)) {
@@ -502,6 +544,11 @@ void BufferCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool keep_page_gpu
     // guest CPU writes come through TryCacheInvalidation, which sends such pages to the GPU thread.
     const DAddr page_begin = Common::AlignDown(device_addr, DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
     const DAddr page_end = Common::AlignUp(device_addr + size, DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+    // EDEN_UP_L1436_ENGINE_TRACKED: decided before the download below, which takes the pages'
+    // GPU-written ranges away; only pages that held none keep their tracking.
+    const bool engine_tracked = engine_write && EngineTrackedOn();
+    const bool page_gpu_data =
+        engine_tracked && gpu_modified_ranges.Intersects(page_begin, page_end - page_begin);
     if (keep_page_gpu_data && VideoCommon::GpuSplit::OwnsScheduler() &&
         gpu_modified_ranges.Intersects(page_begin, page_end - page_begin)) {
         // Switch 2 titles: upload the CPU's bytes into the buffer instead, as CachedWriteMemory
@@ -531,6 +578,14 @@ void BufferCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool keep_page_gpu
             DownloadMemory(page_begin, page_end - page_begin);
         }
     }
+    if (engine_tracked) {
+        if (!page_gpu_data) {
+            NoteEngineTracked(true, memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsWrittenTracked(device_addr, size));
+            MarkVertexBuffersStale(device_addr, size);
+            return;
+        }
+        NoteEngineTracked(false, 0);
+    }
     memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsCpuModified(device_addr, size);
     MarkVertexBuffersStale(device_addr, size);
 }
